	'ab_h1' => 'About Hatoba College',
	'ab_h_b' => 'Hatoba College was founded in 1987 at Port Ellery, and it still teaches on the harbour rather than on a campus set back from the water. The working address is Pier 3, 4 Quay Road, Port Ellery. Harbour Foundation, the 12-week course, is the spine of the year: shore school, simulator bridge, harbour watch, tug and pilot runs, then assessment and berth. Three intakes run each year, in January, April and September, with 18 cadets on a Harbour Foundation intake. The college has not published a count of everyone taught since 1987, so this page does not invent one. What it does state is the present shape of the course, the present fee ledger, and the present staff of seven.',
