	'ab_t4_b' => 'The harbour is the classroom. Paper charts, the simulator, the quay and the workshop are one course, not four products. A number we print is a number we will stand beside: 1987, 18 cadets, three intakes, twelve weeks, the fees in euros, the office hours, and the three dates in the January 2027 cycle. We do not print awards, placement rates, or the names of shipping companies. A place is a letter after interview. A berth is a later letter, after assessment, and only when an operator has a berth to offer. Welfare sits with admissions, in the person of Lucia Ferro, from enquiry to intake. The tone we want on the pier is calm, specific, and easy to check.',
