	'c_t3_r' => 'EEK 12',
	'c_w_b' => 'Week 12 assesses the work the cadet has already practised. The instructors look at a bearing plotted on a paper chart, a watch on the simulator bridge, a harbour watch on Pier 3, and line work from the tug week. The cadet uses the logbook as the record of those weeks. There is no published pass mark and no score released as a ranking. The assessment date for the 12 January 2027 intake is 26 March 2027. After that assessment, a berth that has been arranged is confirmed in writing on the Friday of week 12, which for this intake is 2 April 2027. The application and berth assessment fee is EUR 90, counted inside the programme fee, not added again at week 12.',
