	'in_cap' => 'Seven people at Pier 3',
	'in_h1' => 'Instructors',
	'in_lede' => 'Seven people teach, place, and look after cadets at Hatoba College. Years at sea are stated only where the college has published a figure.',
	'in_note' => 'Seven people',
	'in_s_b' => 'Navigation, simulation, engineering, berths, pilot liaison and welfare are different jobs, and the seven people above keep them distinct. A cadet in weeks 1 to 4 sees the navigation instructor at the chart. In weeks 5 to 7 the simulator lead runs the bridge. Harbour watch on Pier 3 is still instruction, not an unsupervised shift. Week 11 brings in the harbour pilot liaison with the tug crew. The berth placement officer does not teach the bearing, and the admissions officer does not sign the berth letter. The Principal, with 26 years at sea, is the person to whom the week-12 result is accountable. No other sea-time totals are published for this staff list, so none are guessed here.',
	'in_s_sub' => 'How teaching is split',
	'in_t1_i' => 'P',
	'in_t1_r' => 'EOPLE',
	'in_t2_i' => 'T',
	'in_t2_r' => 'EACHING',
	'j_intro' => 'The journal collects college news and course notes from Pier 3. Dates and descriptions live here. Fees, places and berths are confirmed only in the letters those pages describe.',
	'j_n1_b' => 'Posts sit in two categories. College news carries dates: an intake, an open quay, an assessment, a berth Friday. Course notes describe the work, such as a day on the simulator bridge or what the week-12 assessment looks like. Three tags are in use, so you can gather a thread: intake, simulator, and open-quay. The open quay note for 6 February 2027 is college news, tagged open-quay. A simulator piece belongs in course notes, tagged simulator. Intake tags mark anything that hinges on January, April or September, or on the 18 cadets of a Harbour Foundation entry. The journal does not republish the whole fee ledger. For EUR figures, use the programmes page.',
	'j_n1_sub' => 'College news and course notes',
	'j_n2_b' => 'A journal note records a date, a place on Pier 3, or a part of the course. It does not confirm your place, and it does not confirm a berth. Place confirmed comes after enquiry, medical and eyesight check, and interview. Berth confirmed comes in writing on the Friday of week 12, after assessment, and only for a cadet who has a berth arranged. Stories about Noor Haddad, Elias Varga and Joana Prieto stay on the cadet stories page. If a note and a letter ever differ, the letter from admissions or from the berth officer is the one that binds. Questions go to admissions@hatoba-college.example, or to the office on +00 0000 0000, Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 17:00.',
	'j_n2_sub' => 'What a note will not decide',
