	'nf_title' => 'This page is not on the chart.',
	'nl_cap' => 'One email a month',
	'nl_h1' => 'Newsletter',
	'nl_lede' => 'One email a month, from Hatoba College, with intake dates and open quay days. Sending the form opens your own email app. You are not subscribed until that message is sent.',
	'nl_note' => 'One email a month',
	'nl_s_b' => 'Enter your email and send the request. The notice beside the form is this: Opens your email app. Send the request to subscribe; you are not subscribed yet. The message goes to admissions@hatoba-college.example. One address is enough. The college does not ask for a phone number on this form. If you also need to discuss a medical, an eyesight test, or a bursary, use the enquiry form on the admissions page rather than the monthly list. You can unsubscribe by writing to the same address. The office that reads the request is open Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 17:00. A subscription does not reserve a place among the 18 cadets of an intake.',
	'nl_s_sub' => 'How to subscribe',
	'nl_t1_b' => 'The newsletter is one email a month. It carries intake dates and open quay days, and it stays that narrow on purpose. You will see the January, April and September intakes named, and you will see the next first Saturday on the quay, with the hours 10:00 to 13:00. The coming open quay we are telling people about is 6 February 2027. When a Harbour Foundation cycle has fixed milestones, the letter can include them, as with 12 January 2027 for the intake, 26 March 2027 for the assessment, and 2 April 2027 for berth confirmation. The monthly email does not carry a fee change unless the fee ledger on the programmes page has already changed, and it does not carry placement claims.',
