	'pp7_t' => 'Lucia Ferro covers Admissions and cadet welfare, from the first enquiry through the intake and the bursary conversation.',
	'ppl_intro' => 'Seven people teach, place and look after cadets.',
	'ppl_sub' => 'People',
	'pr_apply' => 'Ask about an intake',
	'pr_cap' => 'Seven published fees · EUR',
	'pr_d_b' => 'No. The application and berth assessment is EUR 90, and that deposit is counted in the programme fee when a place is confirmed. You do not add EUR 90 again to Harbour Foundation, to a rating course, or to Deck Officer Preparation. The fee you are shown in the offer is the programme fee with the deposit already inside it, then split into the two instalments. Short-course prices stay as published: EUR 640 for five days of Sea Survival & Fire, and EUR 580 for four days of Radar / ARPA Simulator. If a bursary is later agreed, the offer is rewritten so the remaining instalments are clear. The office can walk through a named programme on any weekday, 08:30 to 17:00.',
	'pr_d_i' => 'D',
	'pr_d_r' => 'EPOSIT',
	'pr_d_sub' => 'Is the assessment fee added on top?',
	'pr_f_b' => 'Harbour Foundation is 12 weeks and costs EUR 4,800. Bridge Watch Rating is 8 weeks and costs EUR 3,600. Engine Room Rating is 10 weeks and costs EUR 4,200. Deck Officer Preparation is 24 weeks and costs EUR 9,200. Sea Survival & Fire is 5 days and costs EUR 640. Radar / ARPA Simulator is 4 days and costs EUR 580. Application and berth assessment is EUR 90. Harbour Foundation takes 18 cadets on each intake. Intake months for the college are January, April and September. The next dated Harbour Foundation intake is 12 January 2027, with assessment on 26 March 2027 and berth confirmation on 2 April 2027. Short courses are booked through admissions and do not replace those intake dates.',
	'pr_f_sub' => 'Fees',
	'pr_h1' => 'Programmes & Fees',
	'pr_i_b' => 'The price on each row is the fee for that programme. It covers instruction for the weeks or days stated, and the facilities that programme uses: shore school and charts, the full-mission bridge simulator, the Pier 3 training berth, the engine room workshop, and the sea-survival pool when the programme includes them. Sea Survival & Fire covers its five days. Radar / ARPA Simulator covers its four days. Deck Officer Preparation covers its 24 weeks of preparation and does not share a single published timetable with the 12-week foundation. The EUR 90 application and berth assessment is a deposit taken when a place is confirmed, and it is counted inside the programme fee. Travel to Port Ellery and living costs while you train are outside the published fee.',
	'pr_i_i' => 'I',
	'pr_i_r' => 'NCLUDED',
	'pr_i_sub' => 'What the fee includes',
	'pr_lede' => 'Seven fees are published in euros, from the 12-week Harbour Foundation to the short courses and the application assessment. A place, once offered, is paid in two instalments.',
	'pr_note' => 'Weeks 1–12 and short courses',
	'pr_p_b' => 'The programme fee is paid in two instalments. Amounts and due dates are written into the offer after a place is confirmed, so the split is not something you calculate from the ledger alone. The EUR 90 deposit is counted inside the fee, not charged again as a third sum. Enquiry does not collect the programme fee. When you write, name the intake you mean: January, April or September. Admissions sends the instalment dates that belong to the offer. Short courses of four or five days follow the same rule of two instalments unless the offer states that the smaller fee is taken in one written payment. Nothing on this page is a discount, a tax figure, or a third-party grant.',
	'pr_p_i' => 'P',
	'pr_p_r' => 'AYMENT',
	'pr_p_sub' => 'Two instalments',
	'pr_t1_i' => 'F',
	'pr_t1_r' => 'EES',
	'pr_u_b' => 'A bursary can be requested when you enquire. It is for a cadet who needs help meeting the published fee. The college does not print a fixed bursary amount, and a bursary is not applied to the ledger on its own. If one is agreed, the sum and the revised instalments appear in the same written offer as the place. Entry still requires age 18 or over, a medical, and an eyesight test, then the interview at Pier 3. A bursary does not confirm a training berth and does not shorten Harbour Foundation, the rating courses, or Deck Officer Preparation. Ask in the enquiry, or by email to admissions@hatoba-college.example, and say which programme and which intake month the request is for.',
	'pr_u_i' => 'B',
	'pr_u_r' => 'URSARY',
	'pr_u_sub' => 'Bursary',
